Subject: [PATCH v2 0/2] ALSA: hda/ca0132: Sound BlasterX AE-5 RGB lighting support

This series adds complete driver support for the RGB lighting systems on
the Creative Sound BlasterX AE-5 and AE-5 Plus sound cards.

The AE-5 hardware contains two distinct RGB lighting zones:
1. External 3-pin 5V addressable RGB header (WS2812B protocol, up to 100 LEDs):
   Driven via the CA0113 PCIe-to-HDA bridge's autonomous DMA link sniffer,
   which snoops a designated 44.1kHz 24-bit playback stream and serializes
   the 24-bit color payload at 800 kHz.
2. On-board logo and shroud accent lighting (APA102 protocol, 5 LEDs):
   Driven directly by CA0113 bridge GPIO pins 2 (data) and 3 (clock) at
   MMIO offset 0x320 on PCIe BAR2.

Both zones are exposed to userspace through volatile card control elements:
  - "AE-5 LED Strip"        (RW, BYTES): 300-byte RGB payload for external strip
  - "AE-5 LED Strip Count"  (RW, INTEGER): Active LED count (1..100)
  - "AE-5 On-Card LEDs"     (RW, BYTES): 15-byte RGB payload for 5 on-board LEDs

Exposing both lighting zones through standard ALSA card controls allows userspace
lighting software (such as OpenRGB) to control the card completely via standard
/dev/snd/controlC* devices, eliminating the need for /dev/mem, PCIe resource sysfs
mmap, or root privileges.

Changes in v2:
  - Updated power management in ae5_strip_send_frame() to use RAII
    CLASS(snd_hda_power_pm, pm)(codec) as suggested by Takashi Iwai.
  - Added patch 2/2 to expose the 5 on-board APA102 LEDs through the matching
    "AE-5 On-Card LEDs" volatile control element.

